portable-tests.sh:   TestTicket223PermissionDeniedSitsInItsOwnSentence    [fixture] ticket 223 AC#4's permission sentence needs a REAL read denial (icacls /deny Everyone:(R)) to plant its premise, and the hosted windows runner session (runneradmin, first red run 43413718734 test-windows step 7) holds an administrator token whose Effective Access ignores a deny ACE on the Everyone group - icacls lands as a no-op, os.ReadFile still succeeds, and the case's own positive control proves the premise absent. Until 2026-11-13 that shape was t.Fatalf('attempt %d: icacls denied nothing...'), i.e. a missing SUBJECT was booked as a broken assertion; the wave-8b leg turned it into a named skip (config_reload_perm_223_windows_test.go) with the reason printed, and it RUNS AND PASSES - all assertions intact - on any host where the deny actually binds (normal-user sessions, the dev box). Re-enable everywhere: a hosted runner image running the step as a non-admin, or a UAC-split-token shape the case could detect; delete the skip branch to return the Fatalf. Accounted by ticket 111 wave 8b (ledger row requested by the dispatch; ticket 71 AC#3 rule that a SKIP must carry a ledger row)
portable-tests.sh:   Test16r1VoiceDemoWakeAsrAgentSpeakSettleRealHardware [fixture] ticket 16 AC#1's demo speaks its reply through the PRODUCTION announce path (real waveOut render, voice_out_windows.go:217); a hosted runner reports zero waveOut output devices, so the D43#15/#26 Speaking walk has no subject there and the announce line degrades to the D10 notification (resident_voice_engines_windows.go:1171) - CI red on run 43425302222 with 'no waveOut output device' + 'timed out waiting for the wav to drain (4.wav)'. The wave-10 leg added the precondition probe demo16AnnounceNeedsAnOutputDevice (voice_e2e_demo_16r1_windows_test.go, openWaveOutSpeaker(22050) per the 26p rig precedent) which SKIPS with that reason only when no device answers; on any machine with an output device the probe closes immediately and every assertion (the whole D43 walk, speak counters, settle trace) runs unchanged - measured PASS on the dev box 2026-11-13. Re-enable everywhere: a runner with any audio endpoint (real or virtual) - delete the probe call to return the unconditional run. Accounted by ticket 111 wave 10 (ledger row requested by the dispatch; ticket 71 AC#3)
portable-tests.sh:   Test41a2r1WarmGateFeedsKwsNotTheAsr                  [fixture] the Warm-gate case measures its turns between KNOWN drain positions of the C8 seam (voice41a2r1Feed), and the seam is a 6-frame/192ms bounded channel whose meter DROPS on overflow and counts it (internal/audio/audio.go:115-145, the 'bounded channel full (slow consumer)' WARN). On a loaded host the ASR hand-off spike (CI run 43425302222: 24.03s, dropped_frames_total=1, kws_hits=1 asr_fed=13312 - the behaviour landed) overruns that window, frames are gone, and the drained counter can never reach the asserted position: the drain timeout is constructively unmeetable, not a behaviour red. The wave-10 leg turned the drain timeout into a verdict helper (voice41a2r1DrainTimeout, resident_voice_41a2r1_windows_test.go): injector Stats() frames_dropped==0 stays a real red (consumer stalled without a seam drop), frames_dropped>0 skips NAMED with the sent/dropped/drained readings. Preconditions in place: it RUNS AND PASSES with all assertions intact (measured on the dev box before the move 2026-11-13). Re-enable everywhere: a host fast enough that the hand-off never overruns 192ms of buffered audio (or an off-thread seam redesign, owner internal/audio). Accounted by ticket 111 wave 10 (ledger row requested by the dispatch; ticket 71 AC#3)
